54,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Looking at the options, Textiles of the Region seems safest. It's local, so it avoids the weight and transport issues.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Textiles has demonstration sessions. My data shows that having people working in the gallery is exactly what brings visitors back.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I like Textiles too! It uses craftspeople, so it doesn't rely on the broken conservation lab as much as City Under Excavation would.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Maritime Trade Routes has too many loans, which means shipping delays. Light and Motion has powered displays, which we know break. Textiles is the way!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Textiles is indeed the most elegant choice. Local garments avoid the transport costs and the exorbitant mount-making fees of larger objects.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, I agree. Light and Motion would also be a nightmare with the evening hire bookings and caterers.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"City Under Excavation has a conservation bench, which sounds great, but @Rin mentioned the lab is overwhelmed. It might be too much.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Yeah, the lab is a mess! Textiles is much more sustainable for the staff we actually have.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Kenji,,And the history circle volunteers would probably love the local weaving stuff! It fits their interests perfectly.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"The logic is inescapable. We avoid the financial drain, the technical failures, and the staffing crisis in one stroke.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I feel comfortable voting for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I concur. It satisfies the visitor's desire for activity while remaining realistic.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Rin,,Me too! Let's pick the one that won't make the staff cry!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm all in for Textiles! No shipping nightmares for me.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I shall join the consensus. It is the only proposal that doesn't invite a budgetary catastrophe.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
